        "original_id": "3054ebcc-8534-57e5-b412-7fa1b98b1d58",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Jesus Jones, The 77s\n- Music releases: Zeroes and Ones, Perverse\n- Organizations: Fools of the World\n- Places: Bradford-on-Avon, Wiltshire, Sacramento, California\n\nFacts:\n- Jesus Jones is a British alternative rock band from Bradford-on-Avon in Wiltshire that formed in late 1988 and recorded and performed from the late 1980s into the 2000s.\n- Zeroes and Ones is the third single from Jesus Jones's 1993 album Perverse.\n- Fools of the World is an independent record label in Sacramento, California that was founded in 1996 by the Christian rock band The 77s.\n- The 77s, also spelled The Seventy Sevens or The 77's, is an American rock band whose lineup includes Michael Roe on vocals and guitar, Mark Harmon on bass, and Bruce Spencer on drums.",
